 succeeded in 118ms:
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:25:<p class="lede">Before an older Dutch building is renovated or demolished, somebody may need to inspect it for asbestos and put a qualified name on the report. <!-- CHECK: 06-bbl-duty --> The apparent business is durable: buy a small certified bureau, keep the inspector, and own the customer book. The dangerous word is <em>keep</em>. A2 Dutch cannot replace the inspector, the technical signatory or the customer lead. One departure can stop production. This essay narrows the pitch to asbestos inventory and asks whether a two-inspector firm can pay both people, acquisition debt and an owner who has left a developer's salary.</p>
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:69:<p>The first number is now a screen. A current employer advertises €2,500–€4,375 gross per month for a 32–40 hour DIA role. <!-- CHECK: 06-dia-salary --> Use a <strong>€75,000 loaded annual retention-cost hurdle</strong> for a senior signing DIA after salary, employer costs, pension, vehicle and equipment. Only the salary range is observed. The loaded amount is deliberately conservative required-price arithmetic.</p>
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:82:<tr><td>Insurance, certification, premises, sales and admin hurdle</td><td>25</td><td>40</td></tr>
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:154:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:25:<p class="lede">The purchase is not a cheap Dutch company. It is cash flow that still exists after the seller leaves, the Dutch account owner stays and acquisition debt is paid. A specialist B2B distributor can fit the reader's capital, languages and engineering habit. It also converts a day job into a leveraged operating job on closing day. The fatal case is simple: “profit” was the retiring owner's unpaid sales labour, customers followed that person, and inventory absorbed the remaining cash. Test the supply edge before searching. Then reject every deal that cannot pay a replacement manager and debt under a flat-sales downside.</p>
chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:66:<p>Every amount below except the Qredits product terms is a design hurdle, not a market price or forecast. The purchase-price hurdle is €300,000: €40,000 buyer cash, a €160,000 senior loan and a €100,000 seller note subordinated until the senior loan is repaid. Lender fees, due diligence and transaction work have a separate €10,000 hurdle. Cash committed is €50,000; no further personal recourse is allowed. KVK describes stacked acquisition finance and gives an example with one-quarter seller-subordinated funding repaid after bank debt. <!-- CHECK: 05-seller-finance --></p>
chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:78:<tr><td>Senior-debt stress: €160k, 9.95%, 60 months</td><td>40.7</td><td>40.7</td></tr>
chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:83:<p>The €40,747 annual senior-debt stress is arithmetic from Qredits' published rate and a 60-month annuity, not a lender quote. <!-- CHECK: 05-qredits-terms --> The year-one owner receives the €90,000 replacement-cost compensation hurdle and owns the €30,300 residual. That reaches the income objective on paper. It leaves the €100,000 seller principal unpaid and therefore does not create distributable wealth without restraint.</p>
chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:145:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
chapters/03-joinery-steel-dossier.html:25:<p class="lede">A small Dutch builder can buy windows from Poland and save money on the object, then lose the saving while matching declarations, performance values and installation evidence to a live project. The proposed business closes that gap in Polish and hands the builder a Dutch-ready evidence pack. Yet the strongest official guidance says correct manufacturer instructions may already give the quality assurer sufficient proof. <!-- CHECK: 03-product-evidence --> Large factories publish documents and sell through distributors. <!-- CHECK: 03-eko-incumbent --> The purchase decision is therefore not “does Wkb create paperwork?” It is whether a builder importing directly will pay a separate fee before one incomplete order delays approval or creates rework.</p>
chapters/03-joinery-steel-dossier.html:70:<tr><td>Pre-order gates</td><td>8 × €2k = 16</td><td>120 × €2k = 240</td></tr>
chapters/03-joinery-steel-dossier.html:84:<p>Year one is a paid experiment beside the job, not owner income. It loses €23,600 after valuing founder time. Cash loss is lower because that labour is not a payroll cheque, but ignoring it would disguise a weak practice. The model has passed only when customers pay both stages without a goods margin subsidising them.</p>
chapters/03-joinery-steel-dossier.html:85:<p>The mature hurdle assumes ten completed orders a month. At twenty-four delivery hours per order, delivery consumes 240 hours monthly. Two coordinators and one quality lead each provide a designed 120 productive hours, leaving one-third of capacity for exceptions, training and absences. The founder sells, handles escalations and maintains supplier relationships. If average delivery exceeds thirty hours, gross margin falls below the intended level before overhead.</p>
chapters/03-joinery-steel-dossier.html:120:<li><strong>Days 40–75:</strong> deliver one paid gate beside the day job. Time supplier chasing, technical judgement, Dutch review and rework separately. Offer the same buyer the €3,000 completion pack before installation; never rebate it through a commission.</li>
chapters/03-joinery-steel-dossier.html:138:<li>Eurostat Comext, <a href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/comext/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/ds-045409?freq=A&amp;reporter=NL&amp;partner=PL&amp;flow=1&amp;indicators=VALUE_IN_EUROS&amp;time=2025&amp;product=7308&amp;product=7610">2025 Netherlands imports from Poland, HS 7308 and 7610</a>.</li>
chapters/03-joinery-steel-dossier.html:145:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:25:<p class="lede">A contractor sprays polyurethane foam or two-part coating. The Dutch exposure limits changed in April 2026, while the crew's training records have already been mandatory for three years. <!-- CHECK: 04-limits --> <!-- CHECK: 04-reach-duty --> The attractive product is one crew, one observed process and one defensible file. The fatal detail is that a model may finish the assessment without measurement, and the reader is not an occupational hygienist. The purchase decision is therefore narrow: will a small contractor pay for a partner-signed assessment and a bilingual operating record, rather than use its existing arbodienst, supplier course and prevention employee?</p>
chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:53:<p>The precedent is Synergy Environmental Solutions in Stoke-on-Trent. Its occupational-hygiene arm markets air and biological isocyanate monitoring for vehicle refinishing, PU foam, adhesive spraying, composites and industrial coating. <!-- CHECK: 04-precedent-offer --> Companies House independently records company 07937140 as active, incorporated on 6 February 2012, with environmental consulting among its activities and accounts through March 2025. <!-- CHECK: 04-precedent-trace --> That proves the service shape can persist elsewhere. It does not transfer British rules, prices or customer behaviour to the Netherlands.</p>
chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:112:<li><strong>Days 40–75:</strong> convert one triage into the €4,750 baseline. Observe a normal job beside the day job, with the hygienist's approved method. Rent instruments only if the assessment calls for measurement. Time founder, technician and hygienist work separately.</li>
chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:133:<li>NVPU, <a href="https://www.nvpu.nl/leden-nvpu/">member directory</a>; a membership view, not a market count.</li>
chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:135:<li>Synergy Environmental Solutions, <a href="https://occupational-hygiene.co.uk/isocyanate-exposure-monitoring/">isocyanate monitoring service</a>; Companies House, <a href="https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/07937140">company 07937140</a>.</li>
chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:139:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
index.html:19:  <p class="lede">Book 4 asked how firms survive. Book 18 asked which technical second business deserves two years and a bounded stake. This book asks the question those two left open: what can a forty-year-old enterprise developer in the Netherlands, with A2 Dutch, three other languages and a hundred thousand euros, earn that does not run on code and still exists in 2030? This is version 0.1. There are no essays yet. There is the method, the reader's edge inventory, ten research memos written by agents from public sources, and a triage of what they found. The essays come after the author's pick.</p>
index.html:67:    <li><a href="research/succession/"><strong>Business succession</strong><span>Sixty listings under €400k, the finance that reaches them, and the rule for which to buy.</span></a></li>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:25:<p class="lede">A cobot arm arrives with papers. The gripper, fixture, program and worker beside it create a different safety question. A small integrator must answer that question before commissioning the cell. The attractive business is a site visit, measured evidence and a file that makes the answer defensible. At least one Dutch welding-cobot case shows the integrator preparing the risk assessment, technical dossier and CE marking. <!-- CHECK: 01-nooteboom --> The manufacturer remains responsible for the declaration. <!-- CHECK: 01-regulation-duties --> The test is whether an integrator will pay an independent specialist to find the dangerous gap while keeping the customer and signature.</p>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:117:<li><strong>Days 20–40:</strong> arrange a calibrated measurement-kit rental and professional-indemnity advice. Spend at most a further <strong>€1,500 hurdle</strong>. Do not buy instruments before a paid site date.</li>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:138:<li>TNO, <a href="https://publications.tno.nl/publication/34645840/IPjRTIJK/TNO-2026-R10389.pdf">Zonder Robotisering verdwijnt de Nederlandse Maakindustrie</a>, 2026.</li>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:145:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
chapters/02-border-files.html:25:<p class="lede">A Dutch steel importer can clear its next load only if the right declarant sits behind the customs entry. Its later carbon bill depends on data held by the foreign mill. That gap appears made for a regulatory reader who can call the supplier in its own language. The fatal point is control. The importer or customs representative keeps the legal role, while a broker can bundle the same data chase into clearance. The first purchase is therefore not a grand compliance retainer. It is one paid supplier-evidence diagnostic, sold through a Dutch declarant, which proves that language can recover better data than the default-value route.</p>
chapters/02-border-files.html:79:<p>Capacity is the real model. Twenty CBAM clients at one delivery day a month consume 240 days a year. Fifteen EUDR clients at half a day consume another 90. Supplier onboardings add about 45 days. One analyst and one associate provide most routine capacity; the founder sells, qualifies, escalates and reviews. If each mill still consumes founder negotiation every quarter, the table has too few people.</p>
chapters/02-border-files.html:112:<li><strong>Days 20–40:</strong> select one product family and create a bilingual supplier request, evidence index and handover pack. Use the customer's existing files. Cap translation, secure storage and professional-insurance advice at a further <strong>€1,500 hurdle</strong>.</li>
chapters/02-border-files.html:141:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
