chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:83:<p>The €40,747 annual senior-debt stress is arithmetic from Qredits' published rate and a 60-month annuity, not a lender quote. <!-- CHECK: 05-qredits-terms --> The year-one owner receives the €90,000 replacement-cost compensation hurdle and owns the €30,300 residual. That reaches the income objective on paper. It leaves the €100,000 seller principal unpaid and therefore does not create distributable wealth without restraint.</p>
chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:85:<p>The kill fact cannot be settled from listings, CBS or lender pages. Only target payroll, bank statements, VAT returns, invoices, stock ageing and an observed owner-task log can show replacement-adjusted cash flow. <!-- CHECK: 05-public-record-limit --> KVK says due diligence must test the seller's information, figures, contracts, staff hours and salaries, and asks whether customers will deal with the buyer. <!-- CHECK: 05-diligence --> Require at least €96,000 annual cash before acquisition debt under flat sales, after the €90,000 CEO replacement line. Below that, or if a 10% gross-profit fall breaks debt service, stop.</p>
chapters/05-owner-independent-acquisition.html:119:<li><strong>Days 55–80:</strong> apply the workbook to three targets. Replace the seller's hours at the €90,000 CEO hurdle, stress gross profit by 10%, map working capital and call no customers without permission. Reject any file that needs post-close “synergy” to pay debt.</li>
